<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abikarib As'ad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 390–420</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> · Also known as As'ad al-Kamil</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abikarib As'ad was a king of Himyar in south <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> in the late 4th and early 5th centuries. Under him Himyar extended its authority into central Arabia through the Kingdom of Kinda, a reach recorded in his inscriptions. Later Arabic tradition remembers him as As'ad <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-kamil">al-Kamil</a>, a conquering king said to have embraced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judaism">Judaism</a>.</p></div>
